sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-memory-12> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Levin argues that the noise and unreliability of biological matter is a feature rather than a bug: morphological and behavioural intelligence arose because of, not in spite of, the vulnerability of the substrate, as suggested by planaria having the noisiest genome and the best regeneration and cancer resistance.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Substrate unreliability is the reason, not an obstacle, for biological intelligence";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Self-Improvising Memory: A Perspective on Memories as Agential, Dynamically Reinterpreting Cognitive Glue”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2024), doi:10.3390/e26060481; section “6. What It Means, and What Next: A Research Program for Further Development”. Scope: Living organisms, especially metazoans"
}
